    {
        "role": "bullet",
        "segment": "Problems encountered when reusing code written by others include increased faults if modifications are made to the original components.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "reused components in which up to 25% of the lines of the original component had been modified had four to eight times more faults than components written from scratch.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "If modifications are made, there may be a need for supplementary techniques such as inspections or extra testing to ensure that the modifications do not introduce unnecessary faults.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Thus, the quality increase promised by reusing components can be further improved if we are careful about how much code we modify. In some cases, we may not be able to avoid changing previously written code; if so, we can use supplementary techniques such as inspections or extra testing to ensure that the modifications do not introduce unnecessary faults.",
                "img_id": null
