        ]
    },
    {
        "role": "bullet",
        "segment": "Objects tend to be small, and the Easier complexity that might ordinarily reside in the component is often pushed instead toward the interfaces among components. This difference means that unit testing is less difficult, but integration testing must be much more extensive.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "Graham also notes which aspects of object orientation make testing easier and which make it harder. For example, objects tend to be small, and the Easier complexity  that  might  ordinarily  reside  in  the  component  is  often  pushed  instead toward the interfaces among components.This difference means that unit testing is less difficult, but integration testing must be much more extensive.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ],
        "type": null
    },
    {
